 section 208 of the Labor-Management Relations Act (Taft-Hartley Act) or section 10 of the Railway Labor Act. • In addition, employment is considered suitable unless the AG member can demonstrate, or the Worker otherwise becomes aware that: o The degree of risk to health and safety is unreasonable;

